 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### engine/group-relay — `implemented`
+
+- When the relay channel of a group call dies (`abort chunk ... Too many
+  retransmissions` after a network blip) the media no longer ends: a new
+  channel is opened on the allocation in force through the same move a new
+  relay uses, three tries (2 s, 4 s apart), and five such recoveries in a row
+  at most. Live, 2026-11-21: a call that went on for the others ended for one
+  device 22 s after its channel died, by the silence watchdog.
+- The audio receive summary names every payload type no demux branch takes
+  (`unknown_by_pt`). Live, 2026-11-21: in group calls most relay packets were
+  payload type 122 and no audio was heard until a rekey; what 122 carries is
+  not known yet.
+
 ### engine/video-state — `implemented`
 
 - A server error ack to one of our `<video>` state stanzas (the stanza's `id`
